// Release-build overlay for the Tauri updater.
//
// NOT referenced by tauri.conf.json, and not committed with real values. The
// committed configuration keeps `plugins.updater.active = false`, so a build
// that nobody has opted in cannot reach an update endpoint at all: the
// frontend treats "not configured" as "updates unavailable" and the user is
// never prompted.
//
// A release pipeline layers this file in:
//
//   tauri build --target x86_64-pc-windows-msvc --bundles nsis \
//     --config src-tauri/tauri.updater.conf.json
//
// Both values below are operator-owned and must come from the build system,
// never from this repository:
//
//   pubkey     the minisign PUBLIC key half of the code-signing key pair used
//              to sign release artifacts and the update manifest. The private
//              key must live in the CI secret store and must never reach a
//              build machine or this repository. A release is only accepted if
//              its manifest verifies against this key, so an attacker who can
//              tamper with the update server still cannot ship a binary.
//
//   endpoints  the HTTPS URL of the update manifest, including the literal
//              {{current_version}} placeholder that Tauri substitutes. It MUST
//              be https:// — an http:// endpoint would let a network attacker
//              serve an unsigned manifest, and the minisign check is the only
//              thing standing between that and arbitrary code execution.
//
// Both are also read from the environment at build time so CI can inject them
// without writing this file to disk:
//
//   AXIS_UPDATER_PUBKEY      -> plugins.updater.pubkey
//   AXIS_UPDATER_ENDPOINTS   -> plugins.updater.endpoints
//
// See docs/DESKTOP.md ("Automatic updates") for the full release checklist.
{
  "plugins": {
    "updater": {
      "active": true,
      "pubkey": "REPLACE_WITH_MINISIGN_PUBLIC_KEY",
      "endpoints": [
        "https://REPLACE_WITH_UPDATE_HOST/axis/{{target}}/{{arch}}/{{current_version}}"
      ]
    }
  }
}
